WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:08.756
One private equity firm spent 60 to 100 hours of senior time
trying to make a general AI assistant run its leadership

00:00:08.756 --> 00:00:09.338
reviews.

00:00:09.578 --> 00:00:10.545
Then it gave up.

00:00:10.785 --> 00:00:14.878
If you are building your firm's next partners, here is what that
firm did instead.

00:00:15.478 --> 00:00:17.120
The firm had done the hard part.

00:00:17.360 --> 00:00:22.774
Its COO had written down, on one page, what a great senior deal
professional does.

00:00:23.014 --> 00:00:28.003
But a framework on paper cannot interview anyone, gather
evidence or write a review.

00:00:28.243 --> 00:00:33.161
The AI assistant could not hold the framework, and what the team
built could not be shared.

00:00:33.761 --> 00:00:38.196
Ask yourself. Do your principals know where they stand on each
competency today?

00:00:38.436 --> 00:00:41.423
And does their feedback reach them in time for the next deal?

00:00:42.023 --> 00:00:43.541
Your framework is the asset.

00:00:43.781 --> 00:00:48.849
It needs a system that interviews your people, gathers the
evidence and drafts the write-up.

00:00:49.089 --> 00:00:50.762
That is why we built CraftArc.

00:00:51.362 --> 00:00:56.647
CraftArc runs your review cycle on your own competency
framework, written in plain English.

00:00:57.247 --> 00:01:01.989
Each person moves through five steps, from launching the review
to a development plan.

00:01:02.589 --> 00:01:07.419
In the self-review, an AI coach interviews each person against
your competencies.

00:01:07.659 --> 00:01:11.782
They answer by voice or text, and the coach asks for whatever is
missing.

00:01:12.382 --> 00:01:16.353
Contributors give anonymous interviews about what they saw
first-hand.

00:01:16.593 --> 00:01:20.886
Every fact is graded as directly observed, hearsay or third
party.

00:01:21.486 --> 00:01:25.649
Before the interviews close, the agent checks coverage for every
competency.

00:01:25.889 --> 00:01:30.476
Here, it warns that nobody who saw the banker meetings has been
heard on sourcing.

00:01:31.076 --> 00:01:35.932
Then it drafts the Executive Committee writeup, the note to the
person and the scorecard.

00:01:36.172 --> 00:01:40.115
If the evidence cannot answer a question, the writeup says so at
the top.

00:01:40.355 --> 00:01:43.547
Your evaluation coordinator owns the final wording.

00:01:44.147 --> 00:01:48.862
That firm now runs its senior deal team on CraftArc, from
principals to partners.

00:01:49.102 --> 00:01:55.332
It signed a 24-month licence, and we built CraftArc with its
COO, who designed the framework.

00:01:55.572 --> 00:02:02.956
Our founder, Dash, worked at McKinsey, Microsoft and Siemens,
and builds AI agents for private equity deal teams.

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:09.170
You start with your senior deal team, and an implementation
consultant adapts the framework to your firm.

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:16.554
One flat annual fee covers every participant and evaluator,
contributors never pay, and there is no build-out fee.

00:02:16.794 --> 00:02:23.013
If we miss a delivery stage and do not fix it, you can leave and
we refund your prepaid fees pro rata.

00:02:23.613 --> 00:02:26.885
If your next review cycle starts in the new year, plan it now.

00:02:27.125 --> 00:02:32.367
Book a demo, bring your competency framework, and we will show
you how it runs on CraftArc.

00:02:32.607 --> 00:02:34.926
This video's voice is AI generated.
